---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const desc = 'Free UPS sizing and battery runtime calculator: kVA from load and power factor, battery kWh for a target runtime, and lithium-ion versus VRLA replacement cost over a 15-year life.';
const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'UPS and Battery Runtime Calculator', applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Web', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  url: 'https://theworldofai.org/calculators/ups-runtime/',
});
---
<Base title="UPS Sizing and Battery Runtime Calculator — The World of AI" description={desc} current="/calculators/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <h1>UPS and Battery Runtime Calculator</h1>
  <p class="answer">A UPS is sized in kVA from the load and its power factor, and the battery is sized in kilowatt-hours from the load and the runtime you need, divided by how deeply the chemistry can be discharged. Lithium-ion is usable to about 80% depth of discharge and lasts 10 to 15 years; VRLA is held to about 50% and replaced every 3 to 5, which is the whole of the cost argument.</p>
  <p class="meta-line">Formula and defaults last reviewed: 2026-08-31.</p>

  <div class="calc">
    <label>Critical load (kW) <input type="number" id="kw" value="500" step="10" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Power factor <input type="number" id="pf" value="0.95" step="0.01" min="0.5" /></label>
    <label>Runtime required (minutes) <input type="number" id="mins" value="10" step="1" min="1" /></label>
    <label>UPS and inverter efficiency (%) <input type="number" id="eff" value="95" step="1" min="50" /></label>
    <label>Battery chemistry
      <select id="chem">
        <option value="0.8|12|1" selected>Lithium-ion, 80% usable, about 12-year life</option>
        <option value="0.5|4|0.55">VRLA, 50% usable, about 4-year life</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <label>Planning horizon (years) <input type="number" id="years" value="15" step="1" min="1" /></label>
    <div class="out" id="out" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </div>

  <h2>How the math works</h2>
  <p>kVA = kW ÷ power factor. Battery energy = (load ÷ inverter efficiency) × runtime in hours,
    because the battery must cover the inverter's losses as well as the load. Installed capacity
    = that energy ÷ usable depth of discharge, since no chemistry is run flat.</p>
  <h2>Why the chemistries differ so much</h2>
  <p>VRLA is cheaper per kilowatt-hour at purchase and is held to roughly half its capacity to
    preserve life, so it needs about 1.6 times the installed capacity for the same runtime, and
    it is replaced three to four times over a fifteen-year facility life. Lithium-ion costs more
    up front, is usable to about 80%, tolerates warmer rooms, and usually outlives one facility
    refresh cycle. Runtime is also only a bridge: it exists to carry the load until generators
    take over, so five to ten minutes is a design choice, not a shortfall.</p>
  <h2>What this does not tell you</h2>
  <p>Real battery runtime is not linear with load, because discharge at high rates yields less
    energy than the rating suggests, an effect described by Peukert's law and captured in
    manufacturer discharge tables rather than in a formula like this. Ambient temperature is the
    other missing variable: VRLA life roughly halves for every 10°C above 25°C.</p>

  <div class="cite-box">Cite this tool: <code>"UPS and Battery Runtime Calculator." The World of AI,
    theworldofai.org/calculators/ups-runtime/.</code></div>

  <script is:inline>
  (function () {
    function n(i) { return parseFloat(document.getElementById(i).value) || 0; }
    function f(v, d) { return v.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: d === undefined ? 0 : d }); }
    var IDS = ['kw','pf','mins','eff','chem','years'];
    function calc() {
      var parts = document.getElementById('chem').value.split('|');
      var dod = parseFloat(parts[0]), life = parseFloat(parts[1]), rel = parseFloat(parts[2]);
      var kva = n('pf') > 0 ? n('kw') / n('pf') : 0;
      var effF = n('eff') > 0 ? n('eff') / 100 : 1;
      var energy = (n('kw') / effF) * (n('mins') / 60);
      var installed = energy / dod;
      var swaps = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(n('years') / life) - 1);
      document.getElementById('out').innerHTML =
        'UPS rating: <b>' + f(kva) + ' kVA</b> for a ' + f(n('kw')) + ' kW load<br>' +
        'Energy to deliver: <b>' + f(energy, 1) + ' kWh</b> at the inverter<br>' +
        'Installed battery capacity: <b>' + f(installed, 1) + ' kWh</b> at ' + f(dod * 100) + '% usable<br>' +
        'Battery replacements in ' + f(n('years')) + ' years: <b>' + swaps + '</b><br>' +
        '<span class="sub">Relative installed cost of this chemistry, lithium-ion as 1.0: about ' + rel.toFixed(2) + ' per kWh, before the replacements above.</span>';
    }
    IDS.forEach(function (i) {
      document.getElementById(i).addEventListener('input', calc);
      document.getElementById(i).addEventListener('change', calc);
    });
    calc();
  })();
  </script>
  <style>
    .calc { border: 1px solid #e6e4de; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; background: #fafaf6; margin: 1.4em 0; }
    .calc label { display: block; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 14px; color: #26262b; }
    .calc input, .calc select { display: block; margin-top: 4px; padding: 7px 9px; font-size: 15px;
      border: 1px solid #cfcdc6; border-radius: 6px; width: 220px; max-width: 100%; }
    .out { margin-top: 14px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid #e6e4de; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .out b { color: #201868; }
    .sub { color: #7A8A9E; font-size: 13.5px; }
  </style>
</Base>
